{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243095-any-edition-when-do-astronomical-solar-eclipses-actually-occur-in-creation","id":1243095,"title":"[Any Edition] When do Astronomical Solar Eclipses actually occur in Creation?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-05T19:35:40-07:00","id":1243095,"title":"[Any Edition] When do Astronomical Solar Eclipses actually occur in Creation?","content":"To clarify: I'm curious about the astronomic events itself <b>in Creation</b>. This is something that's been on my mind. I searched through my 2e &amp; 3E core pdfs, and didn't see any mention. Obviously they happen at some point... But I was curious if there was a calendar specific event, or if it was random, or something else I missed in another book I didn't look up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 08-05-2018, 11:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T19:54:09-07:00","id":1243097,"title":"","content":"If you just google &quot;how often do solar eclipses occur&quot; you got:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Solar eclipses are fairly numerous, </span></span></span><b>about 2 to 4 per year</b><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, but the area on the ground covered by totality is only about 50 miles wide. In any given location on Earth, a total eclipse happens only once every hundred years or so, though for selected locations they can occur as little as a few years apart.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24473-willowfang","name":"Willowfang","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24473_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T20:30:52-07:00","id":1243103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Willowfang</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243095-any-edition-when-do-astronomical-solar-eclipses-actually-occur-in-creation?p=1243097#post1243097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you just google &amp;quot;how often do solar eclipses occur&amp;quot; you got:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Solar eclipses are fairly numerous, </span></span></span><b>about 2 to 4 per year</b><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Roboto\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, but the area on the ground covered by totality is only about 50 miles wide. In any given location on Earth, a total eclipse happens only once every hundred years or so, though for selected locations they can occur as little as a few years apart.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is important to note that Creation does not operate in line with orbital mechanics in any way, shape, or form. The idea that astrological phenomena occur in methods similar to Earth just doesn\u2019t work given the very different nature of the celestial bodies within Creation. <br /> <br /> For the OP, I think the reason they are not set is because that is left to sidereal astrology and the stories told through sidereal chronicles. It\u2019s been a while though since I looked in the 2e or 1E sidereal book though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T20:45:43-07:00","id":1243105,"title":"","content":"When Incarnae feel like it. Back in 1e, at least, the writeup of the Eclipse caste noted that the return of the Solars was the first time that one had occurred since the Usurpation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T20:53:34-07:00","id":1243106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243095-any-edition-when-do-astronomical-solar-eclipses-actually-occur-in-creation?p=1243105#post1243105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When Incarnae feel like it. Back in 1e, at least, the writeup of the Eclipse caste noted that the return of the Solars was the first time that one had occurred since the Usurpation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will look that up. Thanks for the tip!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T22:29:27-07:00","id":1243121,"title":"","content":"Yeah, orbital eclipses are probably uncommon for a flat world where the closest approximation of outer space is a complete abscense of the laws of physics and nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T22:54:04-07:00","id":1243126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243095-any-edition-when-do-astronomical-solar-eclipses-actually-occur-in-creation?p=1243121#post1243121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, orbital eclipses are probably uncommon for a flat world where the closest approximation of outer space is a complete abscense of the laws of physics and nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, for most of the game, it was a sky-dome that you could cut through to get to Hell, with rarefied air requiring special breathing Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T23:16:13-07:00","id":1243129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243095-any-edition-when-do-astronomical-solar-eclipses-actually-occur-in-creation?p=1243126#post1243126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, for most of the game, it was a sky-dome that you could cut through to get to Hell, with rarefied air requiring special breathing Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but a real world eclipse is caused by the sun earth's rotation and the moon just happening to cross between the sun and earth or the earth get between the sun and project the earth's shadow onto the moon. Neither of those really work when neither are in orbit in space around the world and are literally pulled across the sky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T02:19:21-07:00","id":1243152,"title":"","content":"They don't seem to be regularly-scheduled. Per the 3e Core -- &quot;It is said that once her power has passed from the world, Beloved Adorei will return on the next solar eclipse. Yet the next may not happen for another hundred or thousand years, or even longer.&quot; - p.616","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T13:46:55-07:00","id":1243273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243095-any-edition-when-do-astronomical-solar-eclipses-actually-occur-in-creation?p=1243129#post1243129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, but a real world eclipse is caused by the sun earth's rotation and the moon just happening to cross between the sun and earth or the earth get between the sun and project the earth's shadow onto the moon. Neither of those really work when neither are in orbit in space around the world and are literally pulled across the sky.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're high in the sky instead of in space (Bagrash Kol's tower needing gates to let the moon pass was a thing since Bagrash Kol was mentioned) and have &quot;perfect patterning&quot; from being spirits and floating bodies instead of stellar objects (witness Luna's perfect 28 day setup interrupted weirdly by Calibration instead of the real world 29.5 or so day orbital period of the moon). The Wyld, which is sounded like you mentioned, is something different that seeps in at different places. The stars seem to keep it out of their territory and confined to places closer to Creation's ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T16:08:10-07:00","id":1243318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1243095-any-edition-when-do-astronomical-solar-eclipses-actually-occur-in-creation?p=1243273#post1243273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The stars seem to keep it out of their territory and confined to places closer to Creation's ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I think that's a bit too... intricate.<br /> <br /> I have a personal preference for Creation's sky being something that is kind of weird and better off not being thought about too heavily. That, for instance, in a cosmological sense, even though it is finite, there is nothing on the other side of it. <br /> <br /> Similarly, I feel as though the manner in which the Wyld interacts with Creation is most evocative when it's at the edges and consists of a gradual transition of landscapes, so I have a preference for the image of the Wyld only being able to come in at the sides, rather than Creation being a kind of bubble that is being pressed in on from every angle (with the top and bottom just happening to be a lot less permeable).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T15:05:01-07:00","id":1243615,"title":"","content":"These are great thoughts. I had the idea for an Exalted fanfiction SI, where due to shenanigans, the SI is a type of solar destroyed by Cyclene's backlash. The idea I had was a Solar whose caste fluctuates throughout the day. That sounds good at first, but then thematically doesn't work so well with the Eclipse Caste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}